+Shared prefixes across sessions (patches/0310, GLM53_TF_PREFIX_SHARE=1; off by default)
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+Without it a NEW session over a system prompt another session already prefilled resumes only at a snapshot some
+earlier prefill took at or before their common prefix: a GLM53_TF_SESSION_EVERY mark (16,384, 32,768, ...) or the
+fork mark a previous sharer took. The first session never marks its fork point (it has no partner yet), so the
+second session over a system prompt shorter than 16,384 tokens prefills it all (and takes the fork mark the third
+one resumes at). ``PrefixShare`` adds, to the marks rank 0 plans, the position of the prompt's first
+user / assistant / observation role token (everything before it is the system prompt and the tools), on the
+snapshot grid (the page for exact prefills, 64 for fast ones), when it lies in [GLM53_TF_PREFIX_SHARE_MIN (2,048),
